<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/maintain-adequate-calorie-and-carbohydrate-intake-for-individuals-with-type-1-diabetes-on-low-calorie-diet> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Maintain adequate calorie and carbohydrate intake for individuals with type 1 diabetes on low-calorie diet" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "Not specified" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "Not specified" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with type 1 diabetes on low-calorie diet" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "maintain-adequate-calorie-and-carbohydrate-intake-for-individuals-with-type-1-diabetes-on-low-calorie-diet" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Lifestyle" ;
    dmo:statement "Individuals with type 1 diabetes need calories (and carbohydrate) to maintain insulin demands. A low-calorie diet can be harmful as it can induce ketone formation and acidosis. Therefore, there should be an adequate calorie (and carbohydrate) intake to maintain insulin needs (without insulin DKA will develop)." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "Individuals with type 1 diabetes need calories (and carbohydrate) to maintain insulin demands. A low-calorie diet can be harmful as it can induce ketone formation and acidosis. Therefore, there should be an adequate calorie (and carbohydrate) intake to maintain insulin needs (without insulin DKA will develop)." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds-21-metabolic-bariatric-surgery-march-2026> .

<https://example.org/dmo/id/recommendation/measurement-and-communication-of-hba1c-prior-to-surgery> a dmo:Recommendation ;
    rdfs:label "Measurement and communication of HbA1c prior to surgery" ;
    dmo:gradingSystem "CPOC" ;
    dmo:nativeEvidenceGrade "5" ;
    dmo:populationScope "Individuals with diabetes being referred for metabolic-bariatric surgery" ;
    dmo:recommendationId "measurement-and-communication-of-hba1c-prior-to-surgery" ;
    dmo:recommendationStrength "Unspecified" ;
    dmo:recommendationType "Screening" ;
    dmo:statement "HbA1c to be measured and communicated to the specialist metabolic-bariatric surgery MDT coordinator prior to the individual being listed for surgery (within 3 month(s). HbA1c should ideally be 69 mmol/mol (<8.5%) (5) where this can be safely achieved." ;
    dmo:evidenceQuote "HbA1c to be measured and communicated to the specialist metabolic-bariatric surgery MDT coordinator prior to the individual being listed for surgery (within 3 month(s). HbA1c should ideally be 69 mmol/mol (<8.5%) (5) where this can be safely achieved." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://example.org/dmo/id/guidelineSource/jbds-21-metabolic-bariatric-surgery-march-2026> .

